<%--
Action_Menu - overflow "..." dropdown for secondary / destructive actions

default content - the authored menu items (`.dropdown-item` buttons or links).
    Destructive actions (Delete, Disable) belong HERE, inside the menu - never
    as a peer red button next to the primary action.
$label - accessible label for the toggle (default "Actions") [optional]
$align="end" - dropdown alignment: "end" or "start" [optional]

Uses the Bootstrap dropdown (data-bs-toggle). Give items a `$sid` and wire them
in the owning action's on_ready().

Usage:
    <Action_Menu>
        <button $sid="delete_client" class="dropdown-item text-danger" type="button">
            <i class="bi bi-trash"></i> Delete Client
        </button>
    </Action_Menu>
--%>
<Define:Action_Menu tag="div">
    <button type="button" class="Action_Menu__toggle btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary"
            data-bs-toggle="dropdown" aria-expanded="false"
            aria-label="<%= this.args.label || 'Actions' %>">
        <i class="bi bi-three-dots"></i>
    </button>
    <div class="Action_Menu__menu dropdown-menu dropdown-menu-<%= this.args.align || 'end' %>">
        <%= content() %>
    </div>
</Define:Action_Menu>
